{"subjectId":"python","id":"sets","title":"Sets","group":"Data Structures","order":7,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">A <code>set</code> is an unordered collection of unique, hashable items with O(1) membership tests — and real set algebra.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>a = {1, 2, 3, 4}\nb = {3, 4, 5}\nprint(a | b)          # {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}\nprint(a &amp; b)          # {3, 4}\nprint(a - b)          # {1, 2}\nprint(a ^ b)          # {1, 2, 5}\nprint({1, 2} &lt;= a)    # True</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Operator</th><th>Method</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>a | b</code></td><td><code>a.union(b)</code></td><td>In either</td></tr><tr><td><code>a &amp; b</code></td><td><code>a.intersection(b)</code></td><td>In both</td></tr><tr><td><code>a - b</code></td><td><code>a.difference(b)</code></td><td>In <code>a</code> but not <code>b</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>a ^ b</code></td><td><code>a.symmetric_difference(b)</code></td><td>In exactly one</td></tr><tr><td><code>a &lt;= b</code></td><td><code>a.issubset(b)</code></td><td>Every item of <code>a</code> is in <code>b</code></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-plus\"></i>Adding &amp; removing</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>s = set()                  # {} would be an empty *dict*\ns.add(3); s.add(3); s.add(1)\ns.discard(99)              # no error if missing\nprint(sorted(s), len(s))   # [1, 3] 2</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p><code>remove(x)</code> raises <code>KeyError</code> if <code>x</code> is missing; <code>discard(x)</code> doesn't. And <code>{}</code> is an empty <strong>dict</strong> — write <code>set()</code>.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-bulb\"></i>When to reach for a set</h3>\n<div class=\"grid\"><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-filter\"></i>De-duplicate</h3><p><code>list(set(xs))</code> — order is lost; use <code>list(dict.fromkeys(xs))</code> to keep first-seen order.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-bolt\"></i>Fast membership</h3><p><code>x in big_set</code> is O(1) vs O(n) for a list — the difference between TLE and AC.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-route\"></i>Visited nodes</h3><p>BFS / DFS keep a <code>visited</code> set of states or coordinates.</p></div><div class=\"card\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-snowflake\"></i>frozenset</h3><p>An immutable, hashable set — usable as a dict key or inside another set.</p></div></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>xs = [3, 1, 3, 2, 1]\nprint(list(dict.fromkeys(xs)))                   # [3, 1, 2]\ndef has_duplicate(nums):\n    return len(set(nums)) != len(nums)\nprint(has_duplicate(xs), has_duplicate([1, 2]))  # True False</code></pre></figure></section>"}